[38;5;252m[1m## Translation choices worth flagging[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Pointer-heavy code is translated with raw pointers and [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m/[38;5;10mwrapping_sub[0m, mirroring the C line by line. This is deliberate: LZ4 legitimately constructs out-of-range pointers ([38;5;10mbase = source - startIndex[0m) and relies on [38;5;10mu32[0m wraparound in index comparisons, so bounds-checked slices would change behavior. Safe Rust is used where it doesn't affect codegen semantics — the optimal parser's price table is a [38;5;10mVec[0m, and hash/round functions are plain safe arithmetic with explicit [38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Existing C quirks are preserved rather than fixed, for example [38;5;10mctx->end[0m advancing by the full [38;5;10msrcSize[0m in HC [38;5;10mfillOutput[0m mode even when input isn't fully consumed, [38;5;10mLZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict[0m applying the dictionary only once, and [38;5;10mXXH64_digest[0m passing [38;5;10mtotal_len[0m where [38;5;10mmemsize[0m is meant.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mbyPtr[0m table mode is implemented but unreachable on 64-bit, matching the C ([38;5;10msizeof(void*)==4[0m guard).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One caveat on scope: verification covers x86-64 little-endian. The endian-independent paths in the C (big-endian [38;5;10mLZ4_NbCommonBytes[0m, [38;5;10mXXH_swap*[0m) are translated as their little-endian specializations, consistent with the reference build's compile-time selection, so this crate is not portable to big-endian targets.[0m[0m
